\ A local with the name of a global word must not make code compiled for an unrelated helper compile
\ again. `bump` calls the global `count`. `other` binds a local named `count` in its own body, which
\ `bump` cannot see. The trace shows `bump` compiling once however many times `other` runs.

count: ( n -- n ) [ 1 + ] ;

user: ( -- n ) [
  bump: ( n -- n ) [ count 0 + ] ;
  0 3 [ bump ] times
] ;

other: ( k -- n ) [
  count: swap ;
  count
] ;

20 [ user drop 1 other drop ] times
